' RuntimeBudget / TokenBudget lifecycle (migration §5.3) — the bounded-memory
' replacement for CostManager. A funded budget reserves weighted source-token
' events as metered gates fire; the first over-budget reservation fixes a
' canonical out-of-phlo boundary; finalization reports the consensus total_cost;
' reset-from-token re-funds and clears the diagnostic trace. The conservation
' invariant `consumed + remaining == initial` holds in every state.
'
' Source of truth for Figure 5.3 in cost-accounting-migration.md §5.3.
' Palette:  Funded mint #C8E6C9 · Reserving amber #FFECB3 ·
'           OutOfPhlo reject #EF9A9A · Finalized supply-blue #BBDEFB
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/runtime-budget-lifecycle.puml
'          (or: ./render.sh runtime-budget-lifecycle.puml)

@startuml runtime-budget-lifecycle
!theme plain
skinparam defaultFontName "sans-serif"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam state {
  BorderColor #333333
  FontName "sans-serif"
}
title RuntimeBudget / TokenBudget lifecycle — invariant: consumed + remaining == initial

state "Funded\nconsumed = 0\nremaining = initial_tokens" as Funded #C8E6C9
state "Reserving\nreserve_canonical(w)" as Reserving #FFECB3
state "OutOfPhlo\ncanonical OOP boundary fixed\n(first boundary; schedule-independent)" as OOP #EF9A9A
state "Finalized\ntotal_cost = min(consumed, initial)\n(diagnostic digest derived)" as Final #BBDEFB

[*]       --> Funded    : new(initial_tokens)
Funded    --> Reserving : a metered gate fires
Reserving --> Funded    : fits — append billable event,\nconsumed += w
Reserving --> OOP       : would exceed initial →\nfix the FIRST canonical OOP boundary
OOP       --> OOP       : later over-budget attempts\n(first boundary preserved)
Funded    --> Final     : finalization read
OOP       --> Final     : finalization read
Final     --> Funded    : reset_from_token(new initial)\nconsumed := 0; clear trace + OOP

note bottom #E8F5E9
  Invariant (`RuntimeBudgetRefinement.v`): in every state
  **consumed + remaining == initial_tokens**.
  Consensus reads only `total_cost = consumed` (clamped); the cost-trace
  digest / event-count / `last_oop` are diagnostic (TM-CA-151).
  Reconciliation is a pure function of (initial, attempt multiset), so play
  and replay reach the same boundary regardless of scheduling.
end note

@enduml
